WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.790
Cyberspace has a physical
geography: cables,

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.130
data centres, masts and power supplies.

3
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.590
In 2005, 15.6 per cent of the
world's people used the internet.

4
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:16.690
By 2025, it was 73.6 per cent.

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:23.250
In Kenya, access to mobile money lifted
194,000 households out of poverty.

6
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:29.130
Yet the ITU estimates that 2.2
billion people remain offline.

7
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:30.850
No cables where they live?

8
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.150
No interest?

9
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:35.150
So why are so many still offline?

10
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.790
In this mission, you'll see how
cyberspace changed shopping,

11
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.390
money and culture.

12
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.230
Then you'll map the gaps between
who is online and who is not,

13
00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.470
and sort out what causes them.

14
00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.760
Your mission: explain why so
many people are still offline.
